~ start
Patch steps carefully through the laundry basket area. The soft fabric folds rise and fall like gentle hills, and warm light casts long, soft shadows across the colorful socks and small toys scattered around.
The Sock Twins perch on the edge of the basket, peeking down with mischievous grins.
Sock Twin A: Okay, okay… Patch really earned it.
Sock Twin B: Your button rolled right under this laundry basket. We couldn’t lie any longer!
Patch (relieved, eyes wide): You really did see it! Thank you so much.
Patch digs carefully through the folds, feeling the soft cotton and plush, until their tiny hands grasp the missing button.
Stitch the Needle Fairy hovers close, glowing softly. Stitch: Hold still… there. Good as new.
Patch looks down at their chest and smiles, a sense of completeness washing over them. Patch: I feel complete again.
The Sock Twins exchange approving nods, clearly impressed, but still twinkling with their usual mischief.
Narrator: And so, after effort, courage, and a little guidance, Patch’s journey ends here — with a recovered button, a renewed spirit, and friends who are always just a whisper away.
=> END
